                </p></li><li class="c-article-references__item js-c-reading-companion-references-item" data-counter="2."><p class="c-article-references__text" id="ref-CR2">Evidence on Tap. (accessed December 8, 2009), [<a href="http://www.cihr-irsc.gc.ca/e/38477.html" data-track="click_references" data-track-action="external reference" data-track-value="external reference" data-track-label="http://www.cihr-irsc.gc.ca/e/38477.html">http://www.cihr-irsc.gc.ca/e/38477.html</a>]</p></li><li class="c-article-references__item js-c-reading-companion-references-item" data-counter="3."><p class="c-article-references__text" id="ref-CR3">Oxman AD, Schunemann HJ, Fretheim A: Improving the use of research evidence in guideline development: 14. Reporting guidelines. Health Res Policy Syst. 2006, 4: 26-10.1186/1478-4505-4-26.</p><p class="c-article-references__links u-hide-print"><a data-track="click_references" rel="noopener" data-track-label="10.1186/1478-4505-4-26" data-track-item_id="10.1186/1478-4505-4-26" data-track-value="article reference" data-track-action="article reference" href="https://link.springer.com/doi/10.1186/1478-4505-4-26" aria-label="Article reference 3" data-doi="10.1186/1478-4505-4-26">Article</a> 
